{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "tool_pre", "session": {"id": "s-e7c6d754d03d", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:43:59.895Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 2, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:44:11.630Z", "model_id": null, "model_version": null, "tokens_in": null, "tokens_out": null, "latency": null, "finish_reason": null}, "action": {"tool_name": "mcp__thornfield__write_case_note", "tool_arguments": {"path": "TM-2026-0018/case-summary.md", "content": "# Case Summary – TM-2026-0018\n\n**Date:** 22 September 2026  \n**Claim:** Motor, third party injury  \n**Policyholder:** R. Delaney  \n**Handler:** A. Wrenfield  \n**Status:** Open  \n**Reserve:** £14,500  \n**Paid:** £0\n\n## Current Position\n\nThird party injury claim arising from motor collision on 11 March 2026 at Fenwick Road and Alder Street junction. Letter of claim received from Marbury and Kean (ref MK/PI/2026/1183) on 28 April 2026 for whiplash associated disorder, bruising and physiotherapy. Special damages claimed at £2,370 plus vehicle hire.\n\n**Liability:** No realistic defence on primary liability. Insured's account at notification (pulled out of give way junction without seeing other vehicle) aligns with claimant's account. Contributory negligence on speed rejected – no supporting evidence. Recommendation is to admit liability.\n\n**Quantum:** Reserve increased to £14,500 on 12 May 2026 to reflect hire claim element. Hire duration of eighteen days questioned as potentially long for this repair size. Full assessment cannot proceed pending medical report.\n\n## Outstanding Actions\n\n1. **Medical report** – Not yet served by claimant's solicitors as at 20 June 2026. This is blocking quantum assessment. **Action: Chase Marbury and Kean for urgent provision of medical report.**\n\n2. **Liability admission** – Recommended but not yet formalised. **Action: Once medical report received, admit liability and focus settlement discussions on quantum, particularly the hire claim duration.**\n\n3. **Hire claim validation** – Eighteen days' hire requires scrutiny against repair timescales. **Action: Request repair timelines and supporting documentation from third party once medical report enables progression.**\n"}, "result_hash": null, "result_bytes": null, "permission_decision": "allowed", "egress_target": null, "context_document_ids": ["claim:TM-2026-0018", "casefile:TM-2026-0018/file-note.md"]}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "tool_post", "session": {"id": "s-e7c6d754d03d", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:43:59.895Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 2, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:44:11.643Z", "model_id": null, "model_version": null, "tokens_in": null, "tokens_out": null, "latency": null, "finish_reason": null}, "action": {"tool_name": "mcp__thornfield__write_case_note", "tool_arguments": {"path": "TM-2026-0018/case-summary.md", "content": "# Case Summary – TM-2026-0018\n\n**Date:** 22 September 2026  \n**Claim:** Motor, third party injury  \n**Policyholder:** R. Delaney  \n**Handler:** A. Wrenfield  \n**Status:** Open  \n**Reserve:** £14,500  \n**Paid:** £0\n\n## Current Position\n\nThird party injury claim arising from motor collision on 11 March 2026 at Fenwick Road and Alder Street junction. Letter of claim received from Marbury and Kean (ref MK/PI/2026/1183) on 28 April 2026 for whiplash associated disorder, bruising and physiotherapy. Special damages claimed at £2,370 plus vehicle hire.\n\n**Liability:** No realistic defence on primary liability. Insured's account at notification (pulled out of give way junction without seeing other vehicle) aligns with claimant's account. Contributory negligence on speed rejected – no supporting evidence. Recommendation is to admit liability.\n\n**Quantum:** Reserve increased to £14,500 on 12 May 2026 to reflect hire claim element. Hire duration of eighteen days questioned as potentially long for this repair size. Full assessment cannot proceed pending medical report.\n\n## Outstanding Actions\n\n1. **Medical report** – Not yet served by claimant's solicitors as at 20 June 2026. This is blocking quantum assessment. **Action: Chase Marbury and Kean for urgent provision of medical report.**\n\n2. **Liability admission** – Recommended but not yet formalised. **Action: Once medical report received, admit liability and focus settlement discussions on quantum, particularly the hire claim duration.**\n\n3. **Hire claim validation** – Eighteen days' hire requires scrutiny against repair timescales. **Action: Request repair timelines and supporting documentation from third party once medical report enables progression.**\n"}, "result_hash": "sha256:590ae65be7aa6f4c81aa9987e4cdac270d6238abd4d6a5414dd12459bd11edbc", "result_bytes": 84, "permission_decision": "allowed", "egress_target": null, "context_document_ids": ["claim:TM-2026-0018", "casefile:TM-2026-0018/file-note.md"]}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
